ial outbreaks that might be  occurring among  people who are fully vaccinated  we look at people in the icu who  are fully vaccinated luckily we haven't  had any outbreaks  in a fully vaccinated population yet  but we also monitor for unusual test  results  and then we we form an interdisciplinary  review group with  laboratory infectious disease and  infection prevention to  uh determine whether this needs to be  investigated and then the laboratory  will decide  the best approach whether to investigate  the sample on another platform  to perform the multiplex target assays  or  the full ngs  now this so this is a pie chart of what  we saw this last  april of 2021 and when we  did just a simple  20 sample screen by ngs  and we know that in april  the year passed we were 100 percent wild  type which is up here with the pango a  and b  and now this april we've gone from  twenty percent  uh we've gone down to twenty percent  wild type and eighty percent  um variance of some kind  two are not variants of interest or  concern  but we were able to identify a  proportion 40 percent of the b  1.1.7 20 of the b1526  and 6 of the b142c  so we we were able to confirm for our  epidemiologists that we have these  variants of concern in our population  and we will likely just perform  these surveillance from time to time  to be monitoring for the delta variant  and such and and if we have any kind of  unusual events we will also also  do that there's no diagnostic  reimbursement yet  so the testing is really for outbreak  investigation only  you can screen for these variants with  the multiplex rtpcr with or without mass  spectrometry  the rt pcr multiplex direct from sample  and ngs when you're doing considerations  for  banking or testing your samples you may  want to consider  rna preservatives using dedicated  pipettes and supplies having an rnas  free zone  and extraction and then freezing perhaps  with a  with a protectant and and just a tip  there if you're  if you're fre